//// Decision 52 — a condition loop that never breaks answers `null`. Decided
//// 2026-09-18: a loop with no `break <value>` has no value to give, on every
//// backend, and `null` is decision 47's one spelling for absent.
////
//// Measured at `b5a9b85d`:
////
////   commonJS  null   — correct
////   erlang    3      — the loop's variable group leaks out as its value (plus an
////                      `escript` compile warning on stdout: `variable 'I@3' is unused`)
////   wasm      0      — a condition loop still collects, and the empty collection
////                      is read as the integer 0
////   beam      ok     — the atom the last statement answers
////
//// Decision 52's "what it costs" paragraph says erlang and beam print `undefined`;
//// neither does. `undefined` is what they print for a *value* `break` (decision 47),
//// which is a different row.

pub fn main() {
    var i = 0;
    val r = loop (i < 3) { i = i + 1; };
    @print(r);
}
